1
00:00:02,336 --> 00:00:03,879
It is Friday morning

2
00:00:03,962 --> 00:00:05,839
and it is another beautiful day

3
00:00:05,923 --> 00:00:08,842
in Scranton, Pennsylvania.

4
00:00:10,719 --> 00:00:12,513
Oh, my God!

5
00:00:17,559 --> 00:00:20,020
Pick up, pick up, pick up, pick up.

6
00:00:21,855 --> 00:00:24,107
We have a serious problem here.

7
00:00:24,191 --> 00:00:26,431
All right everybody, lock the doors, turn off the lights.

8
00:00:26,485 --> 00:00:27,778
Pretend you're not here.

9
00:00:27,861 --> 00:00:29,530
Are we in danger?

10
00:00:30,572 --> 00:00:33,075
There's no time to think about it, this is real.

11
00:00:34,201 --> 00:00:35,953
Just... Everybody...

12
00:00:41,208 --> 00:00:42,834
Michael, should I call the...

13
00:00:43,335 --> 00:00:44,545
What?

14
00:00:45,420 --> 00:00:50,092
The IT tech guy and me did not get off to a great start.

15
00:01:24,209 --> 00:01:26,169
Yeah, I tried to install it myself,

16
00:01:26,253 --> 00:01:30,215
but you guys have these things so password protected...

17
00:01:30,299 --> 00:01:32,759
That just means you have to enter your password.

18
00:01:33,677 --> 00:01:35,637
What's your password, Michael?

19
00:01:36,013 --> 00:01:39,641
Uh... That's... 1234? Yes.

20
00:01:47,608 --> 00:01:48,609
Michael...

21
00:01:50,360 --> 00:01:51,570
Sorry. Please don't do that.

22
00:01:51,653 --> 00:01:53,172
Okay, I'm sorry. What is going on in there?

23
00:01:53,196 --> 00:01:55,782
Why is he here? What are you doing?

24
00:01:55,949 --> 00:01:58,285
I can't tell you. You have to tell me.

25
00:01:58,368 --> 00:02:00,370
I don't have to tell you anything. Look, Michael,

26
00:02:01,038 --> 00:02:03,332
I know you don't want to have to think about this,

27
00:02:03,415 --> 00:02:05,709
but if something were to happen to you, God forbid,

28
00:02:05,792 --> 00:02:07,711
then I would need to know in order to take over.

29
00:02:07,794 --> 00:02:09,606
Dwight, nothing is going to happen to me, okay?

30
00:02:09,630 --> 00:02:11,715
I'm in the best shape of my life. Look at this.

31
00:02:11,923 --> 00:02:14,027
Yeah, but that doesn't matter, you could get a brain aneurysm...

32
00:02:14,051 --> 00:02:15,528
I'm not going to get... or hit by a car...

33
00:02:15,552 --> 00:02:17,054
Stop. Or a bus or a train.

34
00:02:17,137 --> 00:02:19,657
You could get poisoned, fall down a well, step on a mine, choke.

35
00:02:19,806 --> 00:02:22,619
I'm not... Okay, if I step on a mine in Scranton, Pennsylvania, and die,

36
00:02:22,643 --> 00:02:24,269
you can have my job, okay?

37
00:02:24,353 --> 00:02:25,979
Why don't you just go away?

38
00:02:26,063 --> 00:02:29,900
There are certain things a boss does not share with his employees.

39
00:02:29,983 --> 00:02:32,819
His salary, that would depress them.

40
00:02:33,070 --> 00:02:34,488
His bed.

41
00:02:36,823 --> 00:02:39,868
And I am not going to tell them

42
00:02:39,951 --> 00:02:41,995
that I'll be reading their e-mails.

43
00:02:42,871 --> 00:02:43,955
So how do you search?

44
00:02:44,039 --> 00:02:45,749
By keyword phrase.

45
00:02:46,375 --> 00:02:48,502
Try "profits."

46
00:02:48,669 --> 00:02:50,295
No, try "Michael Scott."

47
00:02:50,712 --> 00:02:55,008
"Michael," "boss" and "funny."

48
00:02:57,219 --> 00:03:00,055
Oh, my God. Wow!

49
00:03:00,847 --> 00:03:02,099
E-mail from Stanley.

50
00:03:02,182 --> 00:03:04,768
Stanley, terribly nice guy.

51
00:03:04,851 --> 00:03:06,353
"Sorry I didn't write back sooner."

52
00:03:06,436 --> 00:03:08,665
"I can't go to the game tonight because my boss, Michael,"

53
00:03:08,689 --> 00:03:10,041
"is an ass and making me stay late."

54
00:03:10,065 --> 00:03:12,401
Well, Stanley's an ass.

55
00:03:12,693 --> 00:03:14,569
Not one of our harder workers.

56
00:03:20,200 --> 00:03:21,451
Hey, what's the deal, Michael?

57
00:03:21,535 --> 00:03:23,328
Why are you spying on our computers?

58
00:03:23,412 --> 00:03:26,873
Oh, no! Everybody, Oscar's gone crazy.

59
00:03:26,957 --> 00:03:28,875
What other ghost stories do you have for us?

60
00:03:29,000 --> 00:03:30,335
That I'm a robot?

61
00:03:32,254 --> 00:03:35,632
I will destroy everything in my path.

62
00:03:35,716 --> 00:03:36,925
Actually, we just...

63
00:03:37,217 --> 00:03:38,760
Actually...

64
00:03:39,010 --> 00:03:40,053
Okay.

65
00:03:41,930 --> 00:03:43,640
Oil can.

66
00:03:44,391 --> 00:03:46,601
Oil can.

67
00:03:46,727 --> 00:03:47,853
Tin Man.

68
00:03:48,395 --> 00:03:50,522
Actually, we just got a memo from IT

69
00:03:50,605 --> 00:03:52,482
saying you're doing e-mail surveillance.

70
00:03:52,566 --> 00:03:55,026
What? No, that defeats the whole purpose.

71
00:03:55,110 --> 00:03:57,237
So it's true? You have access to our e-mails?

72
00:03:57,320 --> 00:03:59,489
You know what the problem is? I think I do.

73
00:03:59,573 --> 00:04:03,410
The problem is that when people hear the term "Big Brother,"

74
00:04:03,493 --> 00:04:06,163
they immediately think it's scary or bad.

75
00:04:06,246 --> 00:04:09,541
But I don't. I think, "Wow, I love my big brother."

76
00:04:09,708 --> 00:04:11,793
I gotta erase a lot of stuff.

77
00:04:12,586 --> 00:04:15,297
A lot of stuff.

78
00:04:16,465 --> 00:04:19,760
Oh, hey. Just so you know, if you have any sensitive e-mails,

79
00:04:19,843 --> 00:04:21,887
they need to be deleted immediately.

80
00:04:21,970 --> 00:04:23,597
I know. Good.

81
00:04:27,100 --> 00:04:28,101
Hey!

82
00:04:31,938 --> 00:04:33,148
Something just happened.

83
00:04:33,231 --> 00:04:35,525
Dwight just told Angela that she has to delete

84
00:04:35,609 --> 00:04:38,028
all of her sensitive e-mails immediately.

85
00:04:38,111 --> 00:04:39,863
What? I know.

86
00:04:41,615 --> 00:04:43,492
Do you think that they're, like... No.

87
00:04:43,575 --> 00:04:45,076
Right. No, no.

88
00:04:50,582 --> 00:04:51,625
Maybe.

89
00:04:51,833 --> 00:04:54,961
It's like squishing a spider under a book.

90
00:04:55,587 --> 00:04:58,256
It's going to be really gross, but I have to look

91
00:04:58,340 --> 00:05:00,634
and make sure that it's really dead.

92
00:05:01,218 --> 00:05:04,304
So if you guys see anything...

93
00:05:05,180 --> 00:05:06,515
Hey, Dwight?

94
00:05:07,724 --> 00:05:10,727
My friend is kind of into these two girls that he works with.

95
00:05:10,811 --> 00:05:11,812
Nice.

96
00:05:11,895 --> 00:05:13,814
One is tall and brunette,

97
00:05:13,897 --> 00:05:17,108
and the other one is short and blond

98
00:05:17,234 --> 00:05:19,778
and perky and kind of judgmental.

99
00:05:20,445 --> 00:05:21,988
Who do you think he should choose?

100
00:05:23,323 --> 00:05:25,784
Does he have access to their medical records?

101
00:05:26,827 --> 00:05:27,828
Um...

102
00:05:29,454 --> 00:05:32,082
I think one of the greatest things about modern America

103
00:05:32,165 --> 00:05:34,584
is the computerization of medical records.

104
00:05:34,668 --> 00:05:38,046
As a volunteer sheriff, I can look up anyone's psychiatric records

105
00:05:38,129 --> 00:05:39,798
or surgical histories.

106
00:05:40,507 --> 00:05:42,008
Yeast infections.

107
00:05:42,092 --> 00:05:46,263
There are a huge number of yeast infections in this county.

108
00:05:47,556 --> 00:05:51,017
Probably because we're downriver

109
00:05:51,935 --> 00:05:53,770
from that old bread factory.

110
00:05:54,187 --> 00:05:58,650
Meredith has an evite from Jim.

111
00:05:58,942 --> 00:06:01,361
Barbeque at Jim's tonight.

112
00:06:01,903 --> 00:06:03,113
Tonight?

113
00:06:03,196 --> 00:06:05,407
Wonder where my evitation is.

114
00:06:05,991 --> 00:06:07,617
Click on guest list.

115
00:06:07,701 --> 00:06:11,288
Angela, Stanley, Oscar, Meredith,

116
00:06:11,371 --> 00:06:14,207
Phyllis, Kevin, Creed.

117
00:06:14,666 --> 00:06:16,459
Must be...

118
00:06:18,420 --> 00:06:19,546
No.

119
00:06:25,385 --> 00:06:27,387
Hey, Angela. How's it going? Hey.

120
00:06:27,470 --> 00:06:28,555
It's okay.

121
00:06:28,638 --> 00:06:31,349
Listen, are you bringing anyone to Jim's party tonight?

122
00:06:31,433 --> 00:06:33,393
No. Are we supposed to?

123
00:06:33,602 --> 00:06:35,896
No. I mean, I don't know. I don't think so.

124
00:06:37,564 --> 00:06:38,899
Excuse me.

125
00:06:51,411 --> 00:06:55,332
There is always a distance between a boss and the employees.

126
00:06:55,415 --> 00:06:58,543
It is just nature's rule.

127
00:06:58,793 --> 00:07:00,295
<i>It's intimidation mostly.</i>

128
00:07:00,378 --> 00:07:03,006
<i>It's the awareness that they are not me.</i>

129
00:07:03,089 --> 00:07:06,760
<i>I do think that I'm very approachable</i>

130
00:07:07,594 --> 00:07:09,721
<i>as one of the guys.</i>

131
00:07:10,430 --> 00:07:12,891
But maybe I need to be even approachabler.

132
00:07:19,522 --> 00:07:22,108
Are you going to eat with us? Of course.

133
00:07:22,692 --> 00:07:25,612
Hanging with my crew, crew that I am one of.

134
00:07:25,987 --> 00:07:29,741
Hanging with my cup of noodles.

135
00:07:30,408 --> 00:07:33,453
This is a meal in a cup. Right here. Hot, tasty.

136
00:07:33,536 --> 00:07:34,955
Reminds me of college.

137
00:07:35,038 --> 00:07:37,499
Lived on this stuff. Brain food.

138
00:07:38,708 --> 00:07:41,044
You know what I really, really miss about college?

139
00:07:41,127 --> 00:07:42,462
The parties.

140
00:07:42,545 --> 00:07:46,800
Everybody would go, the athletes, the nerds, professors.

141
00:07:47,133 --> 00:07:49,052
The professors would go to the parties?

142
00:07:49,135 --> 00:07:51,638
Yeah. They were the most fun.

143
00:07:52,639 --> 00:07:54,307
We always invited them.

144
00:07:56,726 --> 00:07:58,770
<i>It's true, I'm having a party.</i>

145
00:07:59,229 --> 00:08:01,690
I've got three cases of imported beer,

146
00:08:02,107 --> 00:08:05,819
karaoke machine and I didn't invite Michael.

147
00:08:05,986 --> 00:08:08,571
So, three ingredients for a great party.

148
00:08:09,072 --> 00:08:11,512
<i>And it's nothing personal. I just think that if he were there,</i>

149
00:08:11,574 --> 00:08:13,868
<i>people wouldn't be able to relax, you know, have fun.</i>

150
00:08:13,952 --> 00:08:16,329
And my roommate wants to meet everybody.

151
00:08:16,579 --> 00:08:19,332
Because, I'm pretty sure he thinks I'm making Dwight up.

152
00:08:20,959 --> 00:08:22,669
He is very real.

153
00:08:28,299 --> 00:08:29,342
What?

154
00:08:33,013 --> 00:08:35,724
Oh, yes!

155
00:08:35,849 --> 00:08:37,017
Thank you.

156
00:08:43,940 --> 00:08:45,191
Question.

157
00:08:45,275 --> 00:08:47,444
On the Internet, there are several different options

158
00:08:47,527 --> 00:08:49,696
to get to your house for the party tonight,

159
00:08:49,779 --> 00:08:51,823
and I was wondering... Could you keep that down?

160
00:08:52,657 --> 00:08:53,783
Why?

161
00:08:53,867 --> 00:08:55,952
Because not everybody knows about the party.

162
00:08:57,370 --> 00:08:59,372
Like who? Who doesn't know?

163
00:09:00,498 --> 00:09:01,583
Michael.

164
00:09:03,168 --> 00:09:04,502
Why just Michael?

165
00:09:06,713 --> 00:09:08,089
Because it's a surprise.

166
00:09:08,173 --> 00:09:09,507
Is it?

167
00:09:09,758 --> 00:09:11,134
Oh, that's perfect.

168
00:09:11,217 --> 00:09:12,469
So don't tell.

169
00:09:12,552 --> 00:09:14,054
I won't. Okay.

170
00:09:15,430 --> 00:09:18,767
So, Dwight thinks that tonight is a surprise party for Michael.

171
00:09:19,017 --> 00:09:20,727
Really? That's great. I know.

172
00:09:20,810 --> 00:09:22,896
Maybe we can get him to hide and wait somewhere.

173
00:09:24,481 --> 00:09:25,982
Oh, man.

174
00:09:26,274 --> 00:09:28,377
Oh, you know, speaking of which, I was just trying to get

175
00:09:28,401 --> 00:09:31,196
a handle on numbers for food and stuff,

176
00:09:31,279 --> 00:09:33,156
so do you think Roy's gonna come, or...

177
00:09:33,239 --> 00:09:34,991
Oh, no, he can't make it.

178
00:09:35,075 --> 00:09:36,493
Okay, cool.

179
00:09:39,245 --> 00:09:40,955
Hey, there. Hey.

180
00:09:41,247 --> 00:09:43,166
Almost quitting time.

181
00:09:43,249 --> 00:09:45,460
Yep, it's 4:00.

182
00:09:46,169 --> 00:09:50,590
One more hour to take care of anything you forgot to do.

183
00:09:53,218 --> 00:09:56,179
Hey, you know, I don't know if you have any plans tonight,

184
00:09:56,262 --> 00:09:58,431
but if you don't, we could hang out.

185
00:10:00,892 --> 00:10:01,893
Oh, um...

186
00:10:03,561 --> 00:10:04,604
I can't.

187
00:10:04,687 --> 00:10:05,980
You have plans? Yeah, I do.

188
00:10:06,064 --> 00:10:07,357
Yeah? I do, too. I do, too.

189
00:10:07,440 --> 00:10:09,526
You do? Big plans. I do. Yeah.

190
00:10:09,609 --> 00:10:10,795
Because you just said you wanted...

191
00:10:10,819 --> 00:10:12,695
Tonight? I can't do it tonight, no.

192
00:10:12,779 --> 00:10:14,823
Improv class. I have improv class.

193
00:10:14,906 --> 00:10:16,186
Hanging out with my improv buds.

194
00:10:16,241 --> 00:10:17,242
Really? Yeah.

195
00:10:17,325 --> 00:10:18,427
That sounds like a lot of fun.

196
00:10:18,451 --> 00:10:19,953
Oh, it's the best. It is the best.

197
00:10:20,036 --> 00:10:21,704
I would not miss it for the world.

198
00:10:21,788 --> 00:10:24,582
But if something else came up, I would definitely not go.

199
00:10:27,210 --> 00:10:29,003
Improv sounds great.

200
00:10:29,087 --> 00:10:30,630
It is.

201
00:10:35,468 --> 00:10:36,719
Okay.

202
00:10:36,803 --> 00:10:37,887
All right.

203
00:10:39,639 --> 00:10:40,640
What?

204
00:10:41,057 --> 00:10:42,642
I think Stanley just coughed.

205
00:10:51,317 --> 00:10:54,070
Hey, Pam. Do you need me to walk you to your vehicular transport?

206
00:10:54,154 --> 00:10:55,864
No, thanks. All right.

207
00:10:55,989 --> 00:10:57,949
Oscar, got big plans tonight... I'm on a call.

208
00:10:58,032 --> 00:11:01,411
Okay. Kevin. Big man, big man, what are you doing tonight?

209
00:11:01,703 --> 00:11:03,621
Where are you off to? My brother is in town

210
00:11:03,705 --> 00:11:06,708
and we are going to see the Alaska Film Festival...

211
00:11:06,791 --> 00:11:07,959
Okay, all right.

212
00:11:08,042 --> 00:11:12,046
Hey, Angela. Rushie, rushie! Where're you rushing off to?

213
00:11:12,130 --> 00:11:13,232
I'm just leaving for the day.

214
00:11:13,256 --> 00:11:15,175
Yeah, well, duh! Where're you headed?

215
00:11:15,341 --> 00:11:17,468
Charity bake drive.

216
00:11:17,552 --> 00:11:19,220
Liar! You are a liar.

217
00:11:19,304 --> 00:11:20,388
No. No, I'm not!

218
00:11:22,307 --> 00:11:25,143
Dwight! Oh, Dwight, my loyal <i>compadre.</i>

219
00:11:25,310 --> 00:11:27,604
You and I are hanging tonight.

220
00:11:27,687 --> 00:11:31,065
The two of us. We are celebrating our freedom

221
00:11:31,191 --> 00:11:32,567
and our manhood.

222
00:11:32,942 --> 00:11:34,587
You know what? Why don't we watch that show

223
00:11:34,611 --> 00:11:37,697
that you've been wanting to watch? That stupid Battleship Galaxy.

224
00:11:37,780 --> 00:11:38,948
<i>Battlestar Galactica.</i>

225
00:11:39,032 --> 00:11:41,117
That's... Whatever stupid show you want to watch,

226
00:11:41,201 --> 00:11:42,553
we're watching it. I can't tonight.

227
00:11:42,577 --> 00:11:45,496
Unfortunately, I've got plans. I have to go to practice.

228
00:11:45,830 --> 00:11:47,248
Soccer practice.

229
00:11:47,665 --> 00:11:49,542
I didn't know you played soccer, Dwight.

230
00:11:49,834 --> 00:11:50,835
Clarinet.

231
00:11:50,919 --> 00:11:52,128
You, too, Dwight?

232
00:11:53,338 --> 00:11:55,632
Have fun tonight, whatever it is that you're doing,

233
00:11:55,715 --> 00:11:58,384
and I'll see you Monday.

234
00:12:01,054 --> 00:12:02,889
He has no idea.

235
00:12:09,646 --> 00:12:12,124
Quick announcement, everybody, if I could have everybody's attention.

236
00:12:12,148 --> 00:12:13,691
We do have wine in the kitchen

237
00:12:13,775 --> 00:12:16,361
and there is beer available on the porch.

238
00:12:16,611 --> 00:12:17,891
And despite what you might think

239
00:12:17,946 --> 00:12:19,215
it's not all for Meredith and Kelly.

240
00:12:19,239 --> 00:12:21,157
So please enjoy. Jim.

241
00:12:21,574 --> 00:12:23,326
You really think this is a good idea?

242
00:12:23,534 --> 00:12:25,203
A hide-a-key rock?

243
00:12:25,370 --> 00:12:26,788
Hey, you must be Dwight.

244
00:12:26,871 --> 00:12:27,872
You don't work with us.

245
00:12:27,956 --> 00:12:29,499
That's because Mark's my roommate.

246
00:12:30,500 --> 00:12:32,001
Hey, I love the Birkenstocks.

247
00:12:32,085 --> 00:12:33,086
Thanks.

248
00:12:33,419 --> 00:12:36,714
Yeah, I always keep an extra set in the car for special occasions.

249
00:12:37,715 --> 00:12:39,217
Jim, come here.

250
00:12:39,425 --> 00:12:41,219
When is the guest of honor coming?

251
00:12:42,220 --> 00:12:43,972
Oh, laterish.

252
00:12:44,097 --> 00:12:46,224
He's gonna love it. Great.

253
00:12:47,267 --> 00:12:50,204
Just wanna let you guys know that we will be taking the tour like I promised.

254
00:12:50,228 --> 00:12:52,480
Hey. Hey. Just in time.

255
00:12:52,689 --> 00:12:54,708
Do you wanna go on the group tour? We were just about to leave.

256
00:12:54,732 --> 00:12:57,527
Definitely. Well, the group tour is now leaving then.

257
00:12:57,735 --> 00:12:59,213
Ladies and gentlemen, just a few things

258
00:12:59,237 --> 00:13:00,714
that we're going to be pointing out to you today.

259
00:13:00,738 --> 00:13:02,949
You will be able to see both bedrooms

260
00:13:03,032 --> 00:13:04,367
and if we're lucky,

261
00:13:04,450 --> 00:13:06,810
maybe you get a chance to peek into the bathroom, who knows?

262
00:13:06,869 --> 00:13:09,831
I have to remind you also that flash photography is prohibited

263
00:13:09,914 --> 00:13:12,750
and as much as you can, please refrain from touching things.

264
00:13:13,042 --> 00:13:14,460
